Weapons is a 2025 American mystery horror film directed,
written, produced, and co-scored by Zach Cregger.

11
00:59:07,500 --> 00:59:13,500
It stars an ensemble cast including Josh Brolin, Julia Garner, Alden Ehrenreich, Austin
Abrams, Cary Christopher, Toby Huss, Benedict Wong, and Amy Madigan.

12
01:04:30,000 --> 01:04:36,000
Its plot follows the case of seventeen children from the same classroom who
mysteriously run away on the same night at the same time.

13
01:09:52,500 --> 01:09:58,500
After the critical and commercial success of his film Barbarian (2022),
Cregger began working on the spec script for Weapons.

14
01:15:15,000 --> 01:15:21,000
It prompted a bidding war between several studios, with
New Line Cinema emerging as the victor.

15
01:20:37,500 --> 01:20:43,500
The 2023 Hollywood labor disputes disrupted casting.

16
01:26:00,000 --> 01:26:06,000
It initially ran from May to July 2023 before several
actors dropped out due to conflicts.

17
01:31:22,500 --> 01:31:28,500
Casting resumed in February 2024 and ended in May of that year.

18
01:36:45,000 --> 01:36:51,000
Filming then began in Atlanta, concluding in July.

19
01:42:07,500 --> 01:42:13,500
Weapons was released in theaters in the United States
on August 8, 2025, by Warner Bros.

20
01:47:30,000 --> 01:47:36,000
The film received critical acclaim, and was a box office success,
grossing $269 million against a $38 million budget.

21
01:52:52,500 --> 01:52:58,500
Madigan received nominations for an Academy Award and a Golden Globe Award,
and won the Critics Choice Award for Best Supporting Actress.

22
01:58:15,000 --> 01:58:21,000
The film explores themes of witch, small town,
pennsylvania, usa, ritual, junkie.

